**II.2** of Age, **young,** {{Refs 2nd c.BC+|Ostr.Bodl. i237 (2nd c.BC), etc.}}
**III** Adverbial usages,
**III.1** regular _adverb_ σμικρῶς, **but little**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Critias” 107d}}; μικρῶς **by a little**, probably in {{Refs 3rd c.BC+|3rd c.BC: Archimedes Geometra “στομάχιον” 1}}: _superlative_ σμικρότατα {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Memorabilia” 3.11.12.}}
**III.2** σμικροῦ or μικροῦ **within a little, almost**, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|[prev. author] “Cyr.” 1.4.8, 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 18.151, etc.}}; in full, μικροῦ δεῖν, see at {δεῖ} 11, δέω (B) 1; μικροῦ τινος ἀπελείφθη τοῦ μή.. {{Refs 3rd c.AD+|3rd c.AD(?): Achilles Tatius Astronomus 7.13}}; but μικροῦ πρίασθαι **for a little, cheap**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Memorabilia” 2.10.4.}}
**III.3** σμικρῷ **by a little**, with _comparative_, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Politicus” 262c, etc.}}; also σμικρῷ πρόσθεν **a little** before, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|[prev. author] “Lg.” 719b, etc.; μικρῷ ἄνωθεν 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 44.6.}}
**III.4** μικρόν **a little**, σμικρὸν ὑπολείπεσθαι, σμ. τι παρακλίνειν, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Anabasis” 5.4.22, 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Cratylus” 410a}}; of Time, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Anabasis” 3.1.11, etc.; repeated, μικρὸν μικρόν 4th c.BC: Antiphanes Comicus 10: _plural_, of Degree, σμικρὰ γεωμετρίας ἔμπειροι 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Respublica” 527a, etc.; σμίκρ᾽ ἄττα διατρίψαντες [prev. author] “Prt.” 316a; μικρὰ διακινήσω σε περὶ τοῦ πράγματος 3rd c.BC(?): Sosipater Comicus 1.22; περιπάτησον μικρὰ μετ᾽ ἐμοῦ 4th-3rd c.BC: Menander Comicus “Σαμία” 243, compare 1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus “Lucullus” 31.}}
**III.5** with Preps.,
**III.5.a** ἐπὶ σμικρόν **but a little**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Electra” 414, 5th c.BC: Antipho Orator 6.18, 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 4.129.}}
**III.5.b** κατὰ μικρόν **into small pieces**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Anabasis” 7.3.22; so κατὰ μικρὰ γενομένης τῆς δυνάμεως [prev. work] 5.6.32}}; also, **little by little**, κατὰ μικρὸν ἀεί {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Vespae” 702, compare “Nu.” 741}}; opposed to συλλήβδην, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Respublica” 344a}}; καὶ κατὰ σμ. or μ. **ever so little**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|[prev. author] “Sph.” 241c, 5th-6th c.BC: Isocrates Orator 3.10, 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 2.22.}}
**III.5.c** παρὰ μικρόν **within a little**, παρὰ μ. ἐλθεῖν with _infinitive_, to be **within an ace** of doing, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Heraclidae” 295 (_anapaest meter_), compare 5th-6th c.BC: Isocrates Orator 7.6, etc.; παρὰ μ. ἦλθον ἀποθανεῖν [prev. author] 17.42; τὸ παρὰ μ. ὥσπερ οὐδὲν ἀπέχειν δοκεῖ 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Physica” 197a30}}; but τὸ παρὰ μ. σῴζεσθαι to be **only just** saved, {{Refs 6th c.AD+|[prev. author] “Rh.” 1371b11, compare 6th c.AD: Simplicius Philosophus “in Aristotelis Physica commentaria - Comm. in Arist. Graeca” 344.10}}; **gradual, imperceptible** change, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Politica” 1303a20}}; οὐδὲ παρὰ μ. ἦν κρεῖττον with _infinitive_, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|2nd c.BC: Polybius Historicus 12.20.7; [ἡ τύχη] παρὰ μ. εἰς ἑκάτερα ποιεῖ μεγάλας ῥοπάς [prev. author] 15.6.8, compare 5th-6th c.BC: Isocrates Orator 4.59}}; but also παρὰ μ. ποιεῖσθαι, ἡγεῖσθαι, to think **little** of.., {{Refs 5th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 61.51, 5th-6th c.BC: Isocrates Orator 5.79.}}
**III.5.d** μετὰ μικρόν **a little** after, {{NT|NT.Matt.26.73.}}
**IV** besides regular _comparative_ and _superlative_ μικρότερος, -ότατος {{Refs 5th c.BC+|(5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Equites” 789, 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator “Prooemia” 48, etc.), there are the irregular ἐλάσσων, ἐλάχιστος, from ἐλαχύς, and μείων, μεῖστος, also μειότερος}}; see at {μείων. [ῑ} by nature; ῐ only in late Poetry, epigram cited in {{Refs 1st c.AD+|2nd c.AD: Phlegon Trallianus Paradoxographus “fragment” 36.17 1st c.AD: Josephus Historicus]}} (Perh. cf. Latin _mīca_, **mīcidus**, OHG. **smāhi**, ONorse **smár** 'little'.)

