**IV** besides regular _comparative_ and _superlative_ μικρότερος, -ότατος {{Refs 5th c.BC+|(5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Equites” 789, 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator “Prooemia” 48, etc.), there are the irregular ἐλάσσων, ἐλάχιστος, from ἐλαχύς, and μείων, μεῖστος, also μειότερος}}; see at {μείων. [ῑ} by nature; ῐ only in late Poetry, epigram cited in {{Refs 1st c.AD+|2nd c.AD: Phlegon Trallianus Paradoxographus “fragment” 36.17 1st c.AD: Josephus Historicus]}} (Perh. cf. Latin _mīca_, **mīcidus**, OHG. **smāhi**, ONorse **smár** 'little'.)
